---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/welcome-series";
const title = "Shopify email apps for welcome series: workflow guide";
const desc = "Honor the signup promise and guide the next useful action.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Must welcome start with a discount?",
    "answer": "It must honor any promised incentive. Where no incentive was promised, choose content that helps the subscriber’s intended next step."
  },
  {
    "question": "How many messages should I send?",
    "answer": "Use enough to fulfill the promise and support the decision. Evaluate pacing and stopping rules with your own cohorts rather than a universal message count."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should buyers be excluded entirely?",
    "answer": "They may still welcome newsletter content. Remove inaccurate first-order claims and obsolete acquisition nudges while respecting the signup terms."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Welcome series</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email apps for welcome series: workflow guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Honor the signup promise and guide the next useful action.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Record the promise at capture</h2>
      <p>For each form, record its source, offer version, expected content and channel permission. Store the actual incentive terms rather than inferring them from a traffic source or assuming a checkout email is a newsletter signup.</p>
      <p>A quiz result, waitlist request and general newsletter signup have different first-message jobs. Carry useful source metadata into the sender and give missing metadata a neutral fallback.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose one welcome owner</h2>
      <p>List all form tools and senders that can issue welcome messages. Assign a single owner for each promise and use a stable subscription event identifier or equivalent sent state to prevent duplicate enrollment.</p>
      <p>Resubscription needs its own rule. It can acknowledge a return without resetting first-order eligibility. Importing an old list should not automatically replay a new-subscriber series.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Deliver what was offered</h2>
      <p>If the form promises a code or download, make it easy to find and honor the displayed terms. Do not delay the promised benefit to force a brand-story sequence first. Use genuine expiry information rather than an invented countdown.</p>
      <p>Check product eligibility, minimum spend, currency, market and combination behavior at checkout. Give the recipient a help path if the offer fails; sending the correct text is only part of fulfilling the promise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Branch on reliable context</h2>
      <p>Use declared interests or known source intent to choose useful material. Content subscribers might need the next lesson; product researchers might need fit guidance. Do not turn every possible source into a separate maintenance-heavy flow.</p>
      <p>Unknown source should still receive a coherent message. A first-time browser with no purchase record is not necessarily a new customer if historical orders are incomplete. Recheck order history before using first-order claims.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Treat existing customers appropriately</h2>
      <p>A returning customer who subscribes may still value a welcome to the newsletter. Adjust first-purchase language and offer eligibility without assuming they want an immediate replenishment or loyalty pitch.</p>
      <p>An order arriving during the series should stop obsolete acquisition nudges and hand off relevant product onboarding. Preserve the promised signup benefit where its terms still apply; purchase is not permission to ignore the original promise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Coordinate with cart and other senders</h2>
      <p>List actual conflicts between cart offers, welcome benefits and campaign sends. Pause redundant reminders or combine the next useful action while retaining a resume rule. A universal cart-over-welcome hierarchy can hide a code the customer was promised.</p>
      <p>Channel preferences and SMS permission need independent checks. An unopened email is not a sufficient reason to start texting. Coordinate aggregate contact volume and offer terms across every sender.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Build useful content and pace</h2>
      <p>Choose the sequence from the customer’s decision: product use, fit, materials, delivery expectations, returns or relevant customer experience. Link to current information and use a focused next action.</p>
      <p>A high-consideration purchase may need time or consultation; a download subscriber may need immediate access. Treat message count and spacing as hypotheses to evaluate, not a mandatory three-to-five-message recipe or a schedule fixed by vertical.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Evaluate signup cohorts fairly</h2>
      <p>Measure promised-benefit delivery, first purchase, unsubscribes, support issues and net contribution by source. Give cohorts the same observation horizon; this week’s new subscribers have had less time to buy than last month’s.</p>
      <p>Do not equate a high discount-code redemption rate with incremental sales. Propose a controlled comparison of content or cadence while honoring each signup promise. Track later purchases separately rather than booking forecast lifetime revenue as realized profit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Compare tools using your forms</h2>
      <p>Ask each candidate, including the current stack, to show a form submission with metadata, one-time enrollment, a failed-code path and an order arriving during a wait. Confirm exact integrations and plan limits with current primary documentation.</p>
      <p>Estimate contacts, sends, capture tools, SMS where used and operator effort across normal and peak intake. There is no order-volume threshold that alone proves a platform must be replaced.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Cut over without replaying history</h2>
      <p>Proposed rehearsal: fresh signup, returning buyer, repeated form submission, missing source, withdrawn permission and same-session purchase. Record expected messages and exits before running those checks.</p>
      <p>Migrate source and promise versions, enrollment progress and suppression state. Disable the old welcome sender before enabling its replacement, monitor the first cohort and retain a rollback owner. Revisit the map when a form or offer changes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><a class="link" href="/use-cases/segmentation">Audience definitions →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">Post-purchase →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch →</a></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Welcome series FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
